FIXED: Include files (Xilinx TCL scripts, blackbox-supplied HDL sources, and constructor functions for custom bit representations) were emitted once per HDL module rendered after the one that generated them, because the backend's include list is shared between modules and was never cleared. The copies all wrote to the same path, so the generated HDL was correct, but Clash rendered, hashed and wrote them repeatedly and listed each one many times in `clash-manifest.json`. On a large design we measured 126 emitted documents collapse to 50, and the bytes rendered in the HDL-generation phase drop from 31.9 MB to 5.6 MB, halving the time spent rendering and writing HDL.
